From 276220424e46c27d073a4db25ec0a2dcb971849f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 13:51:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/31] crypto: zhihe - select CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519 not the
 _GENERIC symbol

CRYPTO_DEV_ZHIHE selected CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519_GENERIC directly. That
symbol is a bool that "depends on CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519" and is meant to
default-enable once the library is selected; selecting it without the
library it depends on triggers, at every olddefconfig:

  WARNING: unmet direct dependencies detected for CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519_GENERIC
    Depends on [n]: CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519 [=n]
    Selected by [m]: CRYPTO_DEV_ZHIHE [=m] && ...

Select the library symbol CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519 instead; the _GENERIC
implementation then enables itself via its own default. No functional
change to the resulting config (CURVE25519_GENERIC still =y), the spurious
unmet-dependency warning is gone.

Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/crypto/zhihe/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/crypto/zhihe/Kconfig b/drivers/crypto/zhihe/Kconfig
index cc660bbabe6d5..438cd49f9605f 100644
--- a/drivers/crypto/zhihe/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/crypto/zhihe/Kconfig
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ config CRYPTO_DEV_ZHIHE
 	select CRYPTO_SM3
 	select CRYPTO_SM3_GENERIC
 	select CRYPTO_HMAC
-	select CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519_GENERIC
+	select CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519
 	select CRYPTO_LIB_DES
 	select CRYPTO_USER
 	select CRYPTO_USER_API
